---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<Layout title="Writing guide" noindex>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <p class="index-label mb-2">Your writing workspace</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-white">Write. Preview. Publish.</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">Create blog posts, research articles, and tool or project pages entirely in the visual editor.</p>
    <a href={withBase('/write/')} class="mt-6 inline-block rounded-full bg-accent-600 px-5 py-2.5 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-accent-700">Open the editor →</a>
    <section class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-stone-200 p-6 dark:border-stone-800">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">First-time sign-in</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">Only people with access to your repository can save or publish.</p>
      <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
        <li>Open <a class="text-accent-600 underline dark:text-accent-400" href="https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub’s token settings</a> and create a fine-grained token.</li>
        <li>Choose your <strong>cyberpooja.github.io</strong> repository. Allow <strong>Contents</strong> and <strong>Pull requests</strong> to read and write.</li>
        <li>In the editor, select <strong>Sign In with Token</strong> and paste it there. Keep the token private. Sign-in is remembered in this browser until it expires or you sign out.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">From an idea to a published story</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
        <li>Select <strong>Blog</strong>, <strong>Security Research</strong>, or <strong>Tools &amp; Projects</strong>, then create a new entry.</li>
        <li>Add your title, summary, and story. Use the toolbar for formatting, links, images, and code blocks.</li>
        <li>Switch to <strong>Preview</strong> to review your work. Save a draft to return to it later.</li>
        <li>When ready, use the workflow’s <strong>Publish</strong> action. The site updates after the deployment finishes, usually within a few minutes.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Saved drafts stay off the website, but are stored in your public GitHub repository. They are not private documents.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
